#
# prima-materia — the three searches carried in the Zhuzi yulei on 2026-10-10
#
# The file stands on its own and is not appended to another, which is the rule
# in AGENTS.md.
#
# The three questions are the ones the other strand of this run put to the Xiao
# zhiguan: what does the work say makes its own practice fail, does it report a
# case, and does it carry a device that would make the practice unanswerable.
# Putting the same three to a transmission registered as a control is the point
# of having one, and two of the three came back differently.
#
# One finding belongs before the searches because every one of them rests on
# it. This recension writes the word for quiet in two forms, the full form and
# the form with the shortened element, and it uses both for the same word in
# the same juan. The first search of this run was carried in the full form
# alone and returned thirty-three places in thirteen juan; the second form
# returns sixty-three more, in twenty-four juan, seventeen of which the first
# form does not reach at all. Among the places the first form misses are the
# only statement of method in the work, at pmc:ZhuziJingzuoWufa, the whole run
# of affirmative clauses at pmc:ZhuziXuJingzuo, the reported distaste for books
# at pmc:ZhuziYanshuce, the change of mind at pmc:ZhuziHouKanBuran, and the
# second record of both of the work's two cases. A run that had stopped at the
# full form would have reported a transmission that refuses quiet sitting,
# which this one does not, and would have called the refusal a finding.
#

pmp:ZhuziYuleiJingzuoSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "What the Zhuzi yulei says quiet sitting does, and what it says makes it fail"@en, "Was das Zhuzi yulei dem stillen Sitzen zuschreibt und was es scheitern lässt"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Li Jingde (comp.), Zhuzi yulei, 140 juan, in the Wenyuange recension of the Siku quanshu as the Kanseki Repository text KR3a0047 carries it; every occurrence of quiet sitting in both of the spellings the recension uses, read in its surrounding conversation" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Both directions at once, because this transmission gives them in the same conversations: what the work claims for sitting still, with any dose, indication or term it states; and what it names as the way the practice goes wrong, with the consequence. The same question in its failure half was put to the demotic manual at pmp:PdmFailureConditionSearch, to the Clavicula at pmp:ClaviculaFailureConditionSearch, to the gZi brjid at pmp:BonFailureConditionSearch and to the Xiao zhiguan at pmp:XiaoZhiguanFailureConditionSearch." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The practice itself in two spellings over the whole work: the full form of the word for quiet with sitting, thirty-three places in juan 12, 14, 16, 68, 102, 103, 115, 116, 117, 118, 119, 126 and 129; the shortened form with sitting, sixty-three places in juan 9, 11, 12, 16, 23, 26, 31, 45, 52, 59, 63, 64, 74, 80, 96, 102, 104, 113, 114, 115, 120 and 126, of which juan 12 alone carries twenty-three. Ninety-six places in thirty juan in all. Beside them, over the whole work: the word for making an illness, fourteen; sitting in a gallop, two; dull and sleepy, four; the mind dead, four; blank sitting, two; Chan sitting, five; entering absorption, eleven; silent illumination, one; facing the wall, four; demanding the effect, five; forcing the growth, seventy-seven; taking the gain in advance, eight; the word for verify, a hundred and ninety-two, of which the twenty-three places that bear on this practice were read, and its compounds for living a thing through, thirty, and for proof of effect, twenty-three." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:ZhuziDaoliShichu, pmc:ZhuziJingzuoWufa, pmc:ZhuziXuJingzuo, pmc:ZhuziYaojingYueBujing, pmc:ZhuziHunkun, pmc:ZhuziZuowangZuochi, pmc:ZhuziZuobing, pmc:ZhuziXinsiYi, pmc:ZhuziZeXiao, pmc:ZhuziWuwu, pmc:ZhuziChengziShoushi, pmc:ZhuziYanshuce, pmc:ZhuziHouKanBuran, pmc:ZhuziFotuBoundary ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-10" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-10" ;
    skos:note "The finding is the shape of the whole, not any one clause. This transmission states five indications for its practice and no general claim: a beginner, a man weary, the leisure between readings, a man thinking too much, and a man badly agitated. Against them it states that there is no method, that the wanting of the state produces the failure, that the practice taken alone makes an illness, that it is good for a cold constitution and not for everybody, and that a man who keeps still when a matter comes before him has a dead mind. A prescription with five indications, no technique and a contraindication is a different kind of object from anything else in this holding, and it is what the registration of this tradition as a control was for."@en ;
    skos:note "What the other transmissions assign to the practitioner, this one assigns to his wanting, and the difference is worth the entry. At pmc:TiantaiFeiMoSuoWei in the work opened in the other strand of this run the practitioner's want of wisdom carries a harm the method cannot be blamed for; here the practitioner's want of the result is itself the failure, and the method is said to have nothing in it that could have worked instead. The first clears the method, the second has no method to clear."@en ;
    skos:note "Two adverse effects are reported and both are in the work's own terms rather than in a body: a man grew dull and could not think, at pmc:ZhuziHunkun, and a man came away with a distaste for books, at pmc:ZhuziYanshuce. The second is the only entry in this holding in which a practice is reported to have changed what somebody was willing to do, and in a transmission that puts reading and sitting on the same footing that is a result and not a mood."@en .

pmp:ZhuziYuleiCaseReportSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the Zhuzi yulei reports a case of somebody carrying out the practice, with an outcome"@en, "Ob das Zhuzi yulei einen Fall berichtet, in dem jemand die Praxis ausführte, mit Ausgang"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Li Jingde (comp.), Zhuzi yulei, 140 juan, in the Wenyuange recension of the Siku quanshu as the Kanseki Repository text KR3a0047 carries it; the thirty juan carrying the practice in either spelling, read at every place, and juan 129 on the men of the Northern Song read further" ;
    pm:searchedFor "A named or unnamed person said to have carried out the practice, with an outcome: a faculty changed, a state reached, a failure, a harm. Not a doctrinal illustration and not an exemplum. The identical question was put to the Xiao zhiguan in the same run at pmp:XiaoZhiguanCaseReportSearch and came back empty, and the gZi brjid and the demotic manual before it were the same; this is the holding's standing shortage and the reason the question is put first in every work now opened." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The practice in both spellings at all ninety-six places, each read for a person and an outcome; then the word for verify and its compounds at the places where a practitioner is the subject; then the two cases followed into the other juan in which they stand, juan 11 and juan 120. Terms that produced nothing: formerly there was, nil; there once was, nil; so-and-so, nil; proof of effect used of a practitioner of this practice, nil." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:ChenLieJixing, pmc:ZhaoShupingShanEZhiShu, pmc:WuGongjiYiShichen, pmc:ZhuziHuYongYan, pmc:ZhuziYanshuce ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-10" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-10" ;
    skos:note "Five, where every work opened before this one gave none, and the reason is the genre and not the doctrine: this is a record of conversations kept by named disciples over thirty years, so a man who says what happened to him is written down with his name on the entry. The three that are reports of the practice are at pmc:ChenLieJixing, a man who sat a hundred days and could then read at a glance; at pmc:ZhuziHuYongYan, a man who tried the proposition and found the work less in stillness than in movement; and at pmc:ZhuziYanshuce, a man who came away disliking books. The two others are of neighbouring practices: a counted record of thoughts at pmc:ZhaoShupingShanEZhiShu and a borrowed daily hour of stillness at pmc:WuGongjiYiShichen."@en ;
    skos:note "What the five are not. None has a measure, none has a second observer of the outcome, and two of the five are reports about men of an earlier generation rather than about anybody in the room. Two of the five stand twice in the work in two disciples' records, which is a second witness to the report and not to the outcome. They are entered because a case with a name and a duration can be argued with and a transmission's silence cannot, and because the difference between this work and the manuals is now in the holding rather than in a reader's impression of it."@en ;
    skos:note "The three outcomes are of three kinds and the spread is itself the finding: one favourable and large, the reading at a glance; one unfavourable, the distaste for books; one contrary to the doctrine being tested, the work found greater in movement. A transmission that writes down all three is doing something none of the opened manuals does, and it does it without any apparatus for weighing them."@en .

pmp:ZhuziYuleiImmunisationSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the Zhuzi yulei carries a device that would make its practice unanswerable"@en, "Ob das Zhuzi yulei eine Vorrichtung trägt, die seine Praxis unbeantwortbar machen würde"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Li Jingde (comp.), Zhuzi yulei, 140 juan, in the Wenyuange recension of the Siku quanshu as the Kanseki Repository text KR3a0047 carries it; the thirty juan carrying the practice in either spelling, read at every place" ;
    pm:searchedFor "The four devices this holding has met in the opened works, asked for one by one: a guarantee without a condition, of the kind at pmc:TiantaiZheZhang; a rule forbidding the report of the practice's effect or absence, of the kind at generalizations/the-rule-against-reporting-the-absence.ttl; a provision removing the term, so that a failure is never yet due, of the kind at examinations/the-count-that-does-not-fall-due.ttl; and a clause assigning every failure to a person so that none can fall on the procedure, of the kind at generalizations/the-excuse-that-stops-at-the-officiant.ttl." ;
    pm:searchTerms "For the guarantee: will certainly, five, none of them of this practice; without doubt, fifty-eight, read at the places in the thirty juan and all of them of a reading of a text or of a doctrine; the word for proof of effect, twenty-three, read at all of them and none a guarantee of this practice. For the rule against reporting: not to be spoken of outwardly, nil; demanding the effect, five, of which one bears on practice and is entered at pmc:ZhuziZeXiao. For the removed term: the days and months are not to be counted, nil; practise long, read at the places where it occurs in the thirty juan, always as an instruction to persevere at study and never as a bar to judging an outcome. For the displaced failure: forcing the growth, seventy-seven, and taking the gain in advance, eight, read at the places in the thirty juan and entered at pmc:ZhuziYaojingYueBujing." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundNothing ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-10" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-10" ;
    skos:note "None of the four. There is no guarantee for this practice to protect, no prohibition on reporting what came of it, and no provision that keeps a failure from falling due. This is the strongest thing the strand produced and it is a negative: the holding now has one transmission, read at every place where its practice is named, that claims nothing its own failures could contradict. A control is of no use until somebody has asked it the questions the others were asked, and these are the answers."@en ;
    skos:note "Two near misses, because a bare nil would overstate it. At pmc:ZhuziZeXiao the practitioner is forbidden to demand the effect, on pain of a cake gathering in the breast, which is the mirror of the prohibition at pmc:TiantaiZheZhang; what makes it not a device of the fourth kind is that no claim stands behind it, and the passage is about reading. And at pmc:ZhuziYaojingYueBujing the failure is assigned to the practitioner's wanting, which looks like the displacement at pmc:TiantaiFeiMoSuoWei until one sees what is being protected: there, a method that works; here, a method the work says does not exist."@en ;
    skos:note "What this does not settle. Absence over the places where the practice is named is not absence over the work: a hundred and ten juan were not read, and a device of this kind could stand in a conversation that does not use the word. What the search establishes is that at every place this transmission speaks about sitting still, it leaves the question of what came of it open. Whoever reads the rest should start from the juan on the men of the Northern Song and from the instruction of the disciples, where the four devices would most naturally lie."@en .
